{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",

  // Orchestration is the default agent. Its Phase 0 startup check
  // redirects you to the interviewer when there are no active objectives.
  "default_agent": "project-manager"

  // Provider used by this project: openai (built into opencode via
  // Models.dev — no custom npm/baseURL block needed, just OPENAI_API_KEY
  // in the environment, or `opencode auth login`).
  //
  // Every agent runs on the GPT-5.6 family (released 2026-07-09), split
  // across its three tiers by task, not uniformly:
  //
  //   gpt-5.6-sol    Flagship. Reserved for the two low-frequency,
  //                  high-stakes reasoning agents: architect (the plan
  //                  every other agent builds on) and debugger (open-ended
  //                  hypothesis diagnosis on real-world data bugs). Both
  //                  run rarely enough that flagship cost is worth it.
  //
  //   gpt-5.6-terra  Balanced workhorse. Everything else that's invoked
  //                  often and works from an already-specified plan:
  //                  interviewer, project-manager, r-developer,
  //                  r-bugfixer, tester, documenter.
  //
  //   gpt-5.6-luna   Cheapest/fastest tier. doc-backfill only — it's a
  //                  pure dispatcher that inventories files and hands off
  //                  to the documenter; it never writes code or docs
  //                  itself.
  //
  // Which model each agent uses is set directly in the agent .md files.
  // To swap an agent's model when you hit a usage cap, edit its line
  // in config.yaml and run scripts/apply-models.sh to sync it into
  // that agent's .md file — see README "Model Assignments".
  //
  // GPT-5.6 is new as of this writing. If opencode reports a model not
  // found, your local Models.dev snapshot may not have caught up yet —
  // run `opencode models openai --refresh` and cross-check the IDs
  // (gpt-5.6-sol / gpt-5.6-terra / gpt-5.6-luna) against the live catalog
  // before assuming the names above are wrong. If they still don't
  // resolve, pin them explicitly:
  //   "provider": { "openai": { "models": {
  //     "gpt-5.6-sol": {}, "gpt-5.6-terra": {}, "gpt-5.6-luna": {}
  //   } } }
}
